                <pb facs="0780" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/418.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargè Brown to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La Union,
                                Salvador,</hi></placeName><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reports that, on account of health, the President of Nicaragua will be unable to
                    attend the conference, and both countries will be represented <pb facs="0781"
                        n="631" xml:id="pg631"/> by ministers for foreign affairs. The conference
                    should open day after to-morrow. Also reports that advices from Tegucigalpa
                    indicate a disquieting situation because of absence of the recognized
                    responsible Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
